<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers three floater T-bill issues Monday.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers three floater T-bill issues Monday.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer three floating interest T-bill issues with maturities of six, nine and 12 months and a total par of 20 billion levs at auctions on Monday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issues will be offered with no minimum acceptable prices set in advance.</p>
<p>Interest on the issues is due at maturity. It is set equal to the central bank main interest rate for each of the issues and is adjusted every time the rate is changed by the central bank.</p>
<p>The main interest rate is now set at 43.08 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the offers follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3036997024	 BG3037097022</p>
<p> Maturity		 six months	   nine months</p>
<p> Par value		10.0 bln levs	5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	   June 2		 June 2</p>
<p> Issue date	     June 4		 June 4</p>
<p> Maturity date	  December 3	   March 4, 1998</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3037197020</p>
<p> Maturity		 12 months</p>
<p> Par value		5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	   June 2</p>
<p> Issue date	     June 4</p>
<p> Maturity date	  June 3, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
